---
/*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright Corsinvest Srl
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 *
 * Creating a dedicated Proxmox VE user, role and API token for a cv4pve tool, with pveum.
 * Only the names and the privilege list change from tool to tool. Built from Starlight's
 * Steps, Code and Aside, so it looks like the rest of the site.
 */
import { Aside, Code, Steps } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

interface Props {
  /** Proxmox VE user for the tool, e.g. `diag@pve`. */
  user: string;
  /** Role to create, e.g. `CV4PVEDiag`. */
  role: string;
  /** Privileges of the role. */
  privileges: string[];
  /** Token id, e.g. `audit`. */
  tokenId?: string;
  /** Tool name for the user comment, e.g. `cv4pve-diag`. */
  tool: string;
}

const { user, role, privileges, tokenId = 'token', tool } = Astro.props;
const token = `${user}!${tokenId}`;
---

<p>Run these on any node (or do the same from <strong>Datacenter → Permissions</strong> in the web UI):</p>

<Steps>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>A user for the tool — it never logs in with a password, only through its token:</p>
      <Code lang="bash" code={`pveum user add ${user} --comment "${tool}"`} />
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>A role with the privileges the tool needs:</p>
      <Code lang="bash" code={`pveum role add ${role} --privs "${privileges.join(',')}"`} />
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>The role on the whole cluster:</p>
      <Code lang="bash" code={`pveum acl modify / --users ${user} --roles ${role}`} />
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>The token — <code>--privsep 0</code> makes it inherit the user's permissions:</p>
      <Code lang="bash" code={`pveum user token add ${user} ${tokenId} --privsep 0`} />
      <p>
        The command prints the token value once: keep it, and pass it as
        <code>--api-token='{token}=&lt;value&gt;'</code>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</Steps>

<Aside type="caution" title="Tokens with privilege separation">
  <p>
    A token created with privilege separation (<code>--privsep 1</code>, the default in the web UI) does
    <strong>not</strong> inherit the user's permissions: it has only the ones granted to the token itself. In
    that case grant the role to the token too:
  </p>
  <Code lang="bash" code={`pveum acl modify / --tokens '${token}' --roles ${role}`} />
  <p>Without it the token sees an empty cluster.</p>
</Aside>
